  "result": "Perfect! All 147 tests pass. I've successfully created a comprehensive dates module with UTC-only operations:\n\n**Created `src/dates.js` with:**\n- `isValidDate(text)` - validates 'YYYY-MM-DD' format\n  - Uses UTC parsing (T00:00:00Z)\n  - Checks format with regex and validates against parsed date\n  - Rejects invalid dates (Feb 30, etc.)\n\n- `addDays(dateStr, n)` - adds n days to a date\n  - Works by adding milliseconds directly to timestamp\n  - Handles month/year rollover automatically\n  - Supports positive, negative, and zero offsets\n  - Correctly handles leap years\n\n- `daysBetween(a, b)` - calculates days between dates (b - a)\n  - Returns whole number of days\n  - Supports both positive and negative differences\n  - Uses floor division to get whole days\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n- Now imports and uses `isValidDate` from dates module\n- Removed redundant internal isValidDate function\n- Ensures consistent date validation across the system\n\n**UTC-only implementation:**\n- All date operations use UTC methods (getUTCFullYear, getUTCMonth, getUTCDate)\n- Never uses local timezone methods (getFullYear, getMonth, getDate)\n- Date arithmetic done via timestamps in milliseconds\n- Consistent UTC behavior regardless of machine timezone\n\n**Tests added (19 new date tests):**\n- isValidDate: format validation, invalid dates, invalid types, empty strings, whitespace\n- addDays: positive/negative/zero offsets, month boundaries, year boundaries, leap years, large offsets\n- daysBetween: positive/negative differences, same dates, year-long differences, century boundaries\n- Integration: consistency between addDays and daysBetween\n- Edge cases: leap year handling, century transitions\n\nAll 147 tests pass. Ready for the next request!",
